==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tr|ota|سلمك|tr=silmek||to wipe, wash and scrub, rub off or out}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*sīl-||to wipe, rub}}.<ref>{{R:tut-pro:SDM|*sīl-|url=http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2falt%2fturcet&text_number=+723&root=config}}</ref>
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|oui||tr=sil-||to rub}}, {{cog|xqa||tr=sil-||to wipe}}, {{cog|az|silmək||to wipe, erase}}, {{cog|ba|һылау||to smear}}, {{cog|cv|шӑлма||to sweep, wipe, rub}}, {{cog|kk|сылау||to smear, coat}}, {{cog|ky|сылоо}}, {{cog|tk|sylmak|sɨ̄lmak|gloss=to wipe}}, {{cog|tyv|силиир||to become clean}}, {{cog|uz|silamoq||to press, massage}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{tr-verb|siler}}

# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[wipe]], [[wipe up]], [[wipe away]]
# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[rub]] sth. on, [[spread]] something on/over; to [[smear]] sth. on
# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[clean]], [[sweep]], [[rub]], [[rub off]], [[furbish]]
# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[erase]], [[rub out]]
# {{lb|tr|transitive|computing}} to [[delete]]
# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[eat up]] every [[morsel]] of
# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[destroy]], [[sweep]] everything away; to make a clean sweep of, [[get rid of]], [[rule out]]

